course: dictionary
lesson: 3113
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and elect is one of them. Read the words around it to find the meaning that fits. «The class elected Sam as captain.» Here elect means to choose someone by voting.
explain: «She elected to stay at home.» The word to is the clue. When elect is followed by to and a doing word, it means decided or chose to do something. Try swapping in decided: she decided to stay at home. It still makes sense.
explain: «In 2008 Barack Obama was elected the first Black president of the United States.» Elected is a form of elect, and here it means chosen by voting. Elect, elects, elected and electing are all forms of the same word, so look at the ending and the sentence to see what is happening.
explain: Sometimes elect comes after a noun, as in «the president-elect». This means someone who has been chosen for a job but has not started it yet. The word after the noun is the clue that tells you the meaning.
fact: Elect means to choose someone by voting, or to decide to do something.
fact: «Elected» is a form of elect: «Nelson Mandela was elected president in 1994.»
fact: «The Dáil is the main elected house of Ireland's Parliament.» Here elected describes a house whose members were chosen by voting.
fact: «President-elect» means chosen for the job but not yet started in it.
fact: Useful phrases: elect a leader, be elected, elect to do something, newly elected.
exercise: «The class elected Sam as captain.» What does elected mean here? | Lost a race | Taught a lesson | *Chose someone by voting | Painted the goal posts
exercise: «She elected to stay at home.» What does elected to mean here? | Broke a rule | Ran away from home | *Decided or chose to do something | Forgot something
exercise: The mayor is the president-elect. What does president-elect mean? | A person who helps count the votes | A famous president from long ago | *Chosen for the job, but not yet started in it | A president who has left the job
test: Find and copy the word that is a form of elect: «Nelson Mandela was elected president in 1994.» | Nelson | 1994 | *elected | president
test: What does elect mean in «elect a leader»? | Carry the leader | *Choose by voting | Hide the leader | Sing to the leader
exam: Which sentence uses elect to mean decided to do something? | *She elected to read a book instead of going out. | The river elected a new bend. | The team elected Maya as their leader. | Sam elected the red paint for his door.
